From: genshanxinli <127909456+genshanxinli@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 13:19:06 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] net: airoha: write REG_PPE_MTU to all PPEs

airoha_ppe_set_xmit_frame_size() selected a single PPE using the port's
own ingress PPE (!airoha_is_lan_gdm_dev(dev) && airoha_ppe_is_enabled(eth, 1))
and updated only REG_PPE_MTU(ppe_id, index).

However, REG_PPE_MTU(ppe, port_index) constrains the egress frame length
for flows processed by that PPE toward port_index. Cross-domain offloaded
traffic enters through the opposite PPE (LAN/Wi-Fi -> WAN via PPE1,
WAN -> LAN/CPU via PPE2), leaving the active cross-PPE egress MTU registers
stuck at the 1514-byte hardware default and breaking 1518-byte 802.1Q VLAN,
1508-byte PPPoE RFC 4638, and jumbo frames.

In addition, when no netdev on the port is running (for example during
airoha_ppe_hw_init() before interfaces are brought up), len remained 0 and
len += VLAN_ETH_HLEN erroneously wrote 18 into REG_PPE_MTU.

Compute the maximum MTU across all running devices on the physical GDM
port (dropping the per-QDMA filter introduced for single-PPE selection so
sibling devices on different QDMAs cannot clobber the shared egress MTU
with a smaller value), return early when no device is running (!len), and
write REG_PPE_MTU(i, index) to all PPEs (0 .. eth->soc->num_ppe - 1).

Origin: local, xr1710g (#427)
Signed-off-by: genshanxinli <127909456+genshanxinli@users.noreply.github.com>
---
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_ppe.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_ppe.c
@@ -147,34 +147,29 @@ void airoha_ppe_set_xmit_frame_size(stru
 {
 	struct airoha_gdm_port *port = dev->port;
 	struct airoha_eth *eth = dev->eth;
-	struct airoha_qdma *qdma;
-	int i, ppe_id, index;
+	int i, index;
 	u32 len = 0;
 
-	qdma = airoha_qdma_deref(dev);
 	for (i = 0; i < ARRAY_SIZE(port->devs); i++) {
 		struct airoha_gdm_dev *d = port->devs[i];
 		struct net_device *netdev;
-		struct airoha_qdma *q;
 
 		if (!d)
 			continue;
 
-		q = airoha_qdma_deref(d);
-		if (q != qdma)
-			continue;
-
 		netdev = netdev_from_priv(d);
 		if (netif_running(netdev))
 			len = max_t(u32, len, netdev->mtu);
 	}
-	len += VLAN_ETH_HLEN;
+	if (!len)
+		return;
 
-	ppe_id = !airoha_is_lan_gdm_dev(dev) && airoha_ppe_is_enabled(eth, 1);
+	len += VLAN_ETH_HLEN;
 	index = port->id == AIROHA_GDM4_IDX ? 7 : port->id;
-	airoha_fe_rmw(eth, REG_PPE_MTU(ppe_id, index),
-		      FP_EGRESS_MTU_MASK(index),
-		      __field_prep(FP_EGRESS_MTU_MASK(index), len));
+	for (i = 0; i < eth->soc->num_ppe; i++)
+		airoha_fe_rmw(eth, REG_PPE_MTU(i, index),
+			      FP_EGRESS_MTU_MASK(index),
+			      __field_prep(FP_EGRESS_MTU_MASK(index), len));
 }
 
 static void airoha_ppe_hw_init(struct airoha_ppe *ppe)
